# Test: `show pki certificate name` is four commands, one per output form
# VALIDATES: class (e), whole-form alternation -- pem, bundle pem and
#            fingerprint each carry their own usage line, and the detail form
#            keeps the bare path
# PREVENTS: four tail grammars behind one handler switch, which no model can
#           state and no operator can discover from help
#
# The line each form states is the one the MODEL renders. The fingerprint
# algorithm is a closed set the operator types one word of, so it renders as a
# choice and never as a keyword-introduced value.

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze show pki certificate name help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze show pki certificate name <name>
expect=stderr:contains=Commands
expect=stderr:contains=bundle
expect=stderr:contains=fingerprint
expect=stderr:contains=pem
reject=stderr:pattern=bundle pem \| fingerprint

cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze show pki certificate name pem help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze show pki certificate name <name> pem

cmd=foreground:seq=3:exec=ze show pki certificate name bundle pem help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze show pki certificate name <name> bundle pem

cmd=foreground:seq=4:exec=ze show pki certificate name fingerprint help
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stderr:contains=ze show pki certificate name <name> fingerprint [sha256|sha384|sha512]
